# Network Pipeline

Data flows raw → dedupe/merge → normalize → audit → graph → snapshot/export.
Keep it deterministic: no AI/LLM calls anywhere in taxonomy, normalize, dedupe,
similarity or audit. Scores must be reproducible from the same input bytes.

## Determinism & scoring

- Classification is keyword scoring: longer / more specific keywords win.
  `โต๊ะคอมพิวเตอร์` must beat `โต๊ะ`. Don't switch to fuzzy or LLM matching.
- Similarity is char-trigram Jaccard + inverted-index candidates, then union-find.
  Thresholds live in `DEFAULT_CONFIG` (`lib/network/pipeline.ts`), not in routes.
- API routes clamp user input with a `num(value, fallback, min, max)` helper and
  never let a bad body widen the search space.

## Text & Thai handling

- Every product name goes through `lib/network/text.ts`: `repairMojibake` →
  `cleanProductName` → `stripPromo`. Never regex a raw name before repair.
- Use `looksMojibake` to flag, not to silently drop records.
- No stateful global regexes. A `/g` regex with `.test()`/`.exec()` keeps
  `lastIndex` between calls — declare it without `g` or as a per-call literal
  (see `HTML_TAG_TEST`).
- SEO/marketing words (`ญี่ปุ่น`, `มินิมอล`, `มูจิ`, `หรูหรา`, `พรีเมียม`, …) are not
  evidence for style/type. Keep the list in `lib/network/seo-keywords.ts`; mask style
  input and block them in Phrase Memory. Product-type words must not be use_case/function/
  context keywords — use `product_type` + `heuristics.ts` instead.
- Every vocab/taxonomy keyword must pass `npm run audit:keywords`; see
  `lib/network/keyword-registry.ts` and `docs/keyword-audit.md`.

## Types & ids

- `NormalizedProduct` (`lib/network/types.ts`) is the only canonical shape.
  Add fields to the type first; never pass ad-hoc objects between stages.
- Identity is `ext = shopee:{shop_id}:{product_id}`. Heal it from `_raw` when
  the row lost its top-level id columns.
- Category / product-type / brand / province ids are stable snake_case.
  Add keywords or aliases instead of renaming an id — snapshots, edges and
  migrations already reference them.
- An unmatched product type is `*_generic` (e.g. `table_generic`), never `other`.

## Audit

- Each finding costs a capped penalty by severity: critical 45, warning 22,
  info 6. Never double-penalize one finding in two dimensions.
- The `network` dimension score *is* readiness — don't recompute it separately.
- Findings carry actionable Thai messages plus the field they touch.

## Purity & persistence

- `runPipeline(products, config)` is pure and returns `PipelineResult`.
  No DB writes, no file writes inside it.
- Persistence is separate: `saveSnapshot` (`data/network/graph.json`),
  `applyCoreFields` (products sync), `export` route.
- Route handlers that touch disk or DB need `export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'`
  and `export const runtime = 'nodejs'`.
